        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "6a2c5a74-71f8-3fa6-8cc4-03058c772935",
                "word": "expiation",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "223c7644-4389-49e9-8841-e231ec1f3226",
                        "entry_id": "6a2c5a74-71f8-3fa6-8cc4-03058c772935",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "expiations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "26208fd0-18e8-3b9c-92f4-3fe947ddfd86",
                        "entry_id": "6a2c5a74-71f8-3fa6-8cc4-03058c772935",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Action d’expier ou résultat de cette action."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "42388843-55b7-494a-b944-4b29552b968a",
                                "sense_id": "26208fd0-18e8-3b9c-92f4-3fe947ddfd86",
                                "text": "Un si faible châtiment ne suffit pas pour l’expiation de ce crime."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9e00187-2cca-4408-bca2-f0fca747f33a",
                                "sense_id": "26208fd0-18e8-3b9c-92f4-3fe947ddfd86",
                                "text": "Il souffre tout avec patience pour l’expiation de ses péchés."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0e3efb7-4e63-4613-bba4-95eea26cd75f",
                                "sense_id": "26208fd0-18e8-3b9c-92f4-3fe947ddfd86",
                                "text": "En expiation de ses fautes, il s’imposa de..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c04de8c6-60c6-4b5a-be38-e6244a3227b8",
                                "sense_id": "26208fd0-18e8-3b9c-92f4-3fe947ddfd86",
                                "text": "[…] et, comme bien d’autres qui n’oublient jamais les fautes d’autrui, même après expiation, ils ont la mémoire courte pour les services qu’on leur a rendus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5951f1c7-4643-4ad7-a8cd-46997a03400b",
                                "sense_id": "26208fd0-18e8-3b9c-92f4-3fe947ddfd86",
                                "text": "— Il y a dans un livre dont monsieur Lantaigne approuve la doctrine, dans l’illustre Essai sur l’indifférence, une théorie de l’expiation que je vous conseille de lire. J’en ai retenu une phrase que je puis vous rapporter assez exactement : « Une loi fatale, dit Lamennais, une loi inexorable nous presse ; nous ne pouvons échapper à son empire : cette loi, c’est l’expiation, axe inflexible du monde moral, sur lequel roulent toutes les destinées de l’humanité. »"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "291d4f48-e9c4-3ed5-b4db-7e5ff5d619f2",
                        "entry_id": "6a2c5a74-71f8-3fa6-8cc4-03058c772935",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Certaines cérémonies que les Anciens faisaient pour expier un crime ou pour apaiser la colère du ciel, manifestée par les prodiges."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "62a97235-140e-433f-b250-4bf220a025d8",
                                "sense_id": "291d4f48-e9c4-3ed5-b4db-7e5ff5d619f2",
                                "text": "Dans l’ancienne Rome, il y avait des expiations annuelles, pour purifier les villes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76890c11-58da-47b4-8e00-99ab3d6bb50d",
                                "sense_id": "291d4f48-e9c4-3ed5-b4db-7e5ff5d619f2",
                                "text": "Expiations publiques, solennelles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35832876-14a7-4764-bf7e-cc88d14ed807",
                                "sense_id": "291d4f48-e9c4-3ed5-b4db-7e5ff5d619f2",
                                "text": "Sacrifice d’expiation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c40761d0-049d-4965-abe3-9e09d42a0d32",
                        "source_entry_id": "6a2c5a74-71f8-3fa6-8cc4-03058c772935",
                        "source_sense_id": "26208fd0-18e8-3b9c-92f4-3fe947ddfd86",
                        "source_sense_description": "Action d’expier ou résultat de cette action.",
                        "target_lang_word": "atonement",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "atonement",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b33f05e9-38fa-3de0-8917-745317d45e7e",
                                        "entry_id": "620db31c-3a8e-3baa-9fb9-ecd764c9b055",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Making amends to restore a damaged relationship; expiation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f13bab4-da7c-4deb-8a6e-e49e9cf577e9",
                                                "sense_id": "b33f05e9-38fa-3de0-8917-745317d45e7e",
                                                "text": "When a man has been guilty of any vice, the best atonement he can make for it is, to warn others."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d70c999c-1878-4f3d-b236-91c59f2cb17c",
                                                "sense_id": "b33f05e9-38fa-3de0-8917-745317d45e7e",
                                                "text": "1697-1698, John Potter, Archaeologia Graeca\nThe Phocians behaved themselves with so much gallantry, that they were thought to have made a sufficient atonement for their former offense."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fde5a197-fadd-3f9a-b95b-1efa347a2323",
                                        "entry_id": "620db31c-3a8e-3baa-9fb9-ecd764c9b055",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The reconciliation of God and mankind through the death of Jesus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "often",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "671b3720-3edf-31ed-b2a6-a5b080f133be",
                                        "entry_id": "620db31c-3a8e-3baa-9fb9-ecd764c9b055",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Reconciliation; restoration of friendly relations; concord."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7dabe448-c788-434d-b049-aa981bdc91a9",
                                                "sense_id": "671b3720-3edf-31ed-b2a6-a5b080f133be",
                                                "text": "by whom we have now received the atonement"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e389f5cc-5a74-4795-a1f1-f4fd0c0bc18e",
                                                "sense_id": "671b3720-3edf-31ed-b2a6-a5b080f133be",
                                                "text": "He desires to make atonement\nBetwixt the Duke of Gloucester and your brothers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b4441393-4827-42b0-b4d2-257e79f74326",
                        "source_entry_id": "6a2c5a74-71f8-3fa6-8cc4-03058c772935",
                        "source_sense_id": "26208fd0-18e8-3b9c-92f4-3fe947ddfd86",
                        "source_sense_description": "Action d’expier ou résultat de cette action.",
                        "target_lang_word": "expiation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "expiation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "640ae698-5af8-31ef-9fb7-fc9655d4af8a",
                                        "entry_id": "2bebe4a2-9ffd-390a-af9b-f42b38a7f57e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of atonement for a sin or wrongdoing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f4957e8-f1e2-41a1-9868-26ede1848041",
                                                "sense_id": "640ae698-5af8-31ef-9fb7-fc9655d4af8a",
                                                "text": "And see far off below you, where the gulf is fixed, / Your persecutors, in timeless torment, / Parched passion, beyond expiation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f135a4d-7eae-458f-91e7-8a45c1538216",
                                                "sense_id": "640ae698-5af8-31ef-9fb7-fc9655d4af8a",
                                                "text": "One day he came not: I was told, and truly, that business the most imperative required his personal attendance; yet I could not force the ghastly terror of his illness from my mind. I dared not tempt my fate by content—the agony which I suffered seemed a sort of expiation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b498de4d-d710-4f23-9ebe-dc236e95708d",
                                                "sense_id": "640ae698-5af8-31ef-9fb7-fc9655d4af8a",
                                                "text": "Under this plea, felons of the worst kind might claim, till this time, to be taken out of the hands of the law judges, and to be tried at the bishops’ tribunals; and at these tribunals, such a monstrous solecism had Catholicism become, the payment of money was ever welcomed as the ready expiation of crime."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec268826-53e7-3d29-965b-5e01219c7271",
                                        "entry_id": "2bebe4a2-9ffd-390a-af9b-f42b38a7f57e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of expiating or stripping off."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a854112-1931-448e-9ad1-320d8e7595de",
                                                "sense_id": "ec268826-53e7-3d29-965b-5e01219c7271",
                                                "text": "expiation of his immanities fore."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
